        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add deep regression review prototype",
        "body": "Closes #439.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds a default-off OpenClaw deep-regression review prototype with a deterministic high-risk classifier for core/runtime/auth/session/security/provider-routing/release/config surfaces.\n- Adds an optional GitNexus advisory context packet behind `CLAWSWEEPER_GITNEXUS_CONTEXT=1`, including freshness, SHA, byte budget, omitted-context accounting, and secret-like output fail-closed behavior.\n- Extends the decision schema, prompt contract, report frontmatter, public rendering, and close gating with `deepRegressionReview`.\n- Adds context-window telemetry via `CLAWSWEEPER_EXPECTED_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS`; unknown stays `unknown` and no 1M-context claim is made.\n\n## Proof boundary\n\nThis is an advisory prototype. GitHub diff/checkout context remains authoritative, GitNexus context is optional and advisory, stale/missing graph context lowers confidence, and high-risk PRs require explicit proof-boundary reporting. This PR does not claim release safety or bug-free releases.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `node --test test/openclaw-review-risk.test.ts test/gitnexus-context.test.ts test/decision-parser.test.ts test/clawsweeper.test.ts test/close-reasons.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- `pnpm run lint:src && pnpm run lint:scripts`\n- `pnpm run build:repair && node --test test/sweep-workflow.test.ts`\n- `node --test test/apply-label-sync.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run test:unit` - 706 passing, 0 failing\n- `git diff --check`\n\nEvidence packet: `/Volumes/LEXAR/Codex/evidence/clawsweeper-deep-regression/2026-07-09/issue-439/validation.md`\n\n## Review follow-up\n\n- ClawSweeper found a P1 where nonzero GitNexus command stdout/stderr could reach prompt-rendered degraded fields.\n- Fixed by omitting raw failure output, recording only status plus an output hash, and failing closed on secret-like failure output.\n- Added regression tests for nonzero `gitnexus list`, nonzero `gitnexus query`, and secret-like failure output.\n\n## Follow-up notes\n\n- GitNexus auto-refresh is intentionally left for a follow-up ops issue because this prototype should not invent index storage or embedding credentials.\n- PR #432 was rechecked for collision risk before implementation. The overlap is runtime-adjacent around review decision flow, not a direct schema or prompt conflict.\n",
